<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεδνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thin, spare, scanty,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάχνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.219
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.430
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					2.13
				</span></i>
			: later of a person, <i>bald-headed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				25.1
			</span></i>: generally, <i>bare, naked,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					36(48).67
				</span></i>
			(
				Comp.
			):—
				v. l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυδρός</span>
			 or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυδνός</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				122
			</span></i>.</div>
